; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR PI BY THE SPIGOT  -  the digits of pi, one at a time   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, type how many digits (1-1526; Enter alone = 100). The digits
; come out as they are found: 3. then groups of ten, fifty to a line. Y runs
; it again, N quits. Esc quits at any time, even while the digits come.
;
; The Rabinowitz-Wagon spigot: an array of small numbers, all 2 to start, is
; multiplied by 10 and normalised from the far end each pass; the next digit
; falls out of the front. Whole numbers only. Each pass skips the terms that
; no longer matter (half the work), and each pass over the array is raw 1802
; (RUNMC $4730, Firmware-Math/pi_native.asm): no multiply at all, 24-bit
; sums - 18x faster than bytecode. On the Elf2K: 100 digits ~27 s, 300 ~3 min,
; 1000 ~31 min, 1526 ~59 min. Uses $4000-$6FFF (SETSIZE 3). Plain text.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/pi_verify.py, V0061.34): PASS 2026-10-01 - algorithm vs a reference pi for 321 counts up to 1526 (incl. the Feynman point) with the native bounds (q < 128, 24-bit sums, a[i] high byte never $CD); the program's whole transcript byte-exact for 1, 2, 3, 11, 100, 101, 300 and all 1526 digits (59 Elf2K minutes), junk answers, Y/N, and a rerun from dirty RAM.
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-10-01 - Craig: "Pi works."
;
; 275 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 F2 03          SETSIZE 03                         three 4 KB blocks: $4000-$6FFF (the array)
; D 4003 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A                    Ten
; D 4007 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for variables
; D 400B 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 400E 2F 0B 06 6C    WRITEIDX R11 066C                  NBUF ends in a 0
; D 4012 11 0E 03 00    LOADXI R14 0300
; D 4016 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; ASKN:
; D 4018 11 0E 04 D1    LOADXI R14 04D1
; D 401C C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 401E 11 0C 06 6E    LOADXI R12 066E
; D 4022 11 0D 06 6E    LOADXI R13 066E
; D 4026 BD 01 A5       CALL GETL                          Read the line (echoed; backspace works; a lone ESC first quits)
; D 4029 BD 02 9A       CALL PARSE
; D 402C 8C 0D          TESTXZ R13
; D 402E A1 00 38       IFFALSEI PN
; D 4031 11 0A 00 64    LOADXI R10 0064                    Enter alone: the default
; D 4035 B0 00 56       GAL PG
; PN:
; D 4038 86 0D FF FE    TESTXI R13 FFFE
; D 403C A0 00 4D       IFTRUEI PBADN
; D 403F 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 4041 A0 00 4D       IFTRUEI PBADN
; D 4044 11 0C 05 F7    LOADXI R12 05F7
; D 4048 89 AC          TESTLXY R10 < R12
; D 404A A0 00 56       IFTRUEI PG
; PBADN:
; D 404D 11 0E 04 FF    LOADXI R14 04FF
; D 4051 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4053 B0 00 18       GAL ASKN
; PG:
; D 4056 23 00 A9       COPYXY R10 -> R9                   n = digits to print
; D 4059 23 00 98       COPYXY R9 -> R8
; D 405C 52 08 00 06    ADDXI R8 0006                      N = n + GUARD digits computed
; D 4060 23 00 81       COPYXY R8 -> R1
; D 4063 4A 1F          MULTXY R1 * R15
; D 4065 21 11          COPYAX MA -> R1
; D 4067 11 06 00 03    LOADXI R6 0003
; D 406B 4D 16          DIVXY R1 / R6
; D 406D 25             COPYMAA
; D 406E 21 01          COPYAX Acc -> R1
; D 4070 52 01 00 04    ADDXI R1 0004                      L = 10 N / 3 + MARGIN terms
; D 4074 11 0E 08 06    LOADXI R14 0806
; D 4078 3A 02 1E       COPYXMY R1 -> M(R14)               L for the native INIT
; D 407B F1 47 00       RUNMC 4700                         a[1..L] = 2, in raw 1802
; D 407E 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000                     no passes yet
; D 4082 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000                    nothing printed
; D 4086 11 0C 00 00    LOADXI R12 0000                    no nines held
; D 408A 11 0D FF FF    LOADXI R13 FFFF                    no digit held
; D 408E 11 0E 05 28    LOADXI R14 0528
; D 4092 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; PASS:
; D 4094 CC             SERST
; D 4095 A1 00 AD       IFFALSEI PASS0                     a key? only a lone ESC matters: it stops and quits
; D 4098 CB             SERIN
; D 4099 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B
; D 409C A1 00 AD       IFFALSEI PASS0
; D 409F BD 01 E1       CALL GETLW
; D 40A2 A1 01 9A       IFFALSEI STOPQ
; D 40A5 CB             SERIN                              an arrow (ESC [ x): its two bytes are thrown away
; D 40A6 BD 01 E1       CALL GETLW
; D 40A9 A1 00 AD       IFFALSEI PASS0
; D 40AC CB             SERIN
; PASS0:
; D 40AD 87 A9          TESTXY R10 = R9
; D 40AF A0 01 4B       IFTRUEI FIN                        all the digits asked for are out
; D 40B2 87 78          TESTXY R7 = R8
; D 40B4 A0 01 34       IFTRUEI FLUSH                      N passes done (a long run of 9s): print what is held
; D 40B7 51 87 01       SUBXYZ R8 - R7 -> R1
; D 40BA 4A 1F          MULTXY R1 * R15
; D 40BC 21 11          COPYAX MA -> R1
; D 40BE 11 06 00 03    LOADXI R6 0003
; D 40C2 4D 16          DIVXY R1 / R6
; D 40C4 25             COPYMAA
; D 40C5 21 01          COPYAX Acc -> R1
; D 40C7 52 01 00 04    ADDXI R1 0004                      i = 10 (N - passes) / 3 + MARGIN: the terms that still matter
; D 40CB 11 0E 08 04    LOADXI R14 0804
; D 40CF 3A 02 1E       COPYXMY R1 -> M(R14)               TOP for the native PASS
; D 40D2 F1 47 30       RUNMC 4730                         the whole pass in raw 1802: a[TOP..1], then a[1] = q mod 10
; D 40D5 2E 0B 08 08    READIDX R11 0808
; D 40D9 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4                   R4 = the new digit (0-10)
; D 40DB 42 07          INCX R7
; D 40DD 86 04 00 09    TESTXI R4 0009
; D 40E1 A1 00 E9       IFFALSEI N9
; D 40E4 42 0C          INCX R12                           a 9: held with the others
; D 40E6 B0 00 94       GAL PASS
; N9:
; D 40E9 86 04 00 0A    TESTXI R4 000A
; D 40ED A1 01 10       IFFALSEI NORM
; D 40F0 23 00 D6       COPYXY R13 -> R6
; D 40F3 42 06          INCX R6
; D 40F5 BD 01 FA       CALL OUTD
; Z0:
; D 40F8 8C 0C          TESTXZ R12
; D 40FA A0 01 09       IFTRUEI Z1
; D 40FD 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 4101 BD 01 FA       CALL OUTD
; D 4104 43 0C          DECX R12
; D 4106 B0 00 F8       GAL Z0
; Z1:
; D 4109 11 0D 00 00    LOADXI R13 0000                    and 0 is held
; D 410D B0 00 94       GAL PASS
; NORM:
; D 4110 86 0D FF FF    TESTXI R13 FFFF
; D 4114 A0 01 2E       IFTRUEI NH                         the very first digit: nothing held yet
; D 4117 23 00 D6       COPYXY R13 -> R6
; D 411A BD 01 FA       CALL OUTD
; N90:
; D 411D 8C 0C          TESTXZ R12
; D 411F A0 01 2E       IFTRUEI NH
; D 4122 11 06 00 09    LOADXI R6 0009
; D 4126 BD 01 FA       CALL OUTD
; D 4129 43 0C          DECX R12
; D 412B B0 01 1D       GAL N90
; NH:
; D 412E 23 00 4D       COPYXY R4 -> R13                   this digit is held
; D 4131 B0 00 94       GAL PASS
; FLUSH:
; D 4134 23 00 D6       COPYXY R13 -> R6
; D 4137 BD 01 FA       CALL OUTD
; FL9:
; D 413A 8C 0C          TESTXZ R12
; D 413C A0 01 4B       IFTRUEI FIN
; D 413F 11 06 00 09    LOADXI R6 0009
; D 4143 BD 01 FA       CALL OUTD
; D 4146 43 0C          DECX R12
; D 4148 B0 01 3A       GAL FL9
; FIN:
; D 414B 11 0E 05 3A    LOADXI R14 053A
; D 414F C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4151 23 00 9A       COPYXY R9 -> R10
; D 4154 BD 02 48       CALL NUM
; D 4157 11 0E 05 49    LOADXI R14 0549
; D 415B C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 415D 11 0E 05 58    LOADXI R14 0558
; D 4161 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; AW:
; D 4163 CC             SERST
; D 4164 A1 01 63       IFFALSEI AW
; D 4167 CB             SERIN
; D 4168 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10
; D 416A 86 0A 00 79    TESTXI R10 0079
; D 416E A0 01 90       IFTRUEI YES
; D 4171 86 0A 00 59    TESTXI R10 0059
; D 4175 A0 01 90       IFTRUEI YES
; D 4178 86 0A 00 6E    TESTXI R10 006E
; D 417C A0 01 95       IFTRUEI NO
; D 417F 86 0A 00 4E    TESTXI R10 004E
; D 4183 A0 01 95       IFTRUEI NO
; D 4186 86 0A 00 1B    TESTXI R10 001B
; D 418A A0 01 95       IFTRUEI NO
; D 418D B0 01 63       GAL AW
; YES:
; D 4190 CA 59          SEROUTI 59 'Y'                     echo it
; D 4192 B0 00 18       GAL ASKN
; NO:
; D 4195 CA 4E          SEROUTI 4E 'N'
; D 4197 B0 01 9E       GAL BYEQ
; STOPQ:
; D 419A CA 0D          SEROUTI 0D
; D 419C CA 0A          SEROUTI 0A
; BYEQ:
; D 419E 11 0E 05 6C    LOADXI R14 056C
; D 41A2 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 41A4 00             HALT
; GETL:
; GETLK:
; D 41A5 CB             SERIN                              the first key
; D 41A6 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B
; D 41A9 A1 01 BD       IFFALSEI GETLN
; D 41AC BD 01 E1       CALL GETLW                         ESC: an arrow following?
; D 41AF A1 01 9E       IFFALSEI BYEQ                      no: ESC on its own quits
; D 41B2 CB             SERIN                              an arrow (ESC [ x): its two bytes are thrown away
; D 41B3 BD 01 E1       CALL GETLW
; D 41B6 A1 01 A5       IFFALSEI GETLK
; D 41B9 CB             SERIN
; D 41BA B0 01 A5       GAL GETLK
; GETLN:
; D 41BD 81 00 0D       TESTAI 000D
; D 41C0 A1 01 CB       IFFALSEI GETLC
; D 41C3 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 41C6 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)      Enter alone: the empty line
; D 41C9 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLC:
; D 41CB 81 00 08       TESTAI 0008
; D 41CE A0 01 A5       IFTRUEI GETLK                      nothing to rub out yet
; D 41D1 81 00 7F       TESTAI 007F
; D 41D4 A0 01 A5       IFTRUEI GETLK
; D 41D7 C9             SEROUT                             the echo
; D 41D8 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)
; D 41DB 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 41DD C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the rest of the line (Backspace can rub out the first key too)
; D 41DF BE 00          RETURN
; GETLW:
; D 41E1 72 09          PUSHX R9
; D 41E3 11 09 00 08    LOADXI R9 0008
; GETLW1:
; D 41E7 CC             SERST
; D 41E8 A0 01 F2       IFTRUEI GETLW2
; D 41EB 43 09          DECX R9
; D 41ED 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 41EF A1 01 E7       IFFALSEI GETLW1
; GETLW2:
; D 41F2 73 09          POPX R9
; D 41F4 CC             SERST                              Test: a key is waiting
; D 41F5 BE 00          RETURN
; D 41F7 F0 00 00       BREAK
; OUTD:
; D 41FA 87 A9          TESTXY R10 = R9
; D 41FC A0 02 46       IFTRUEI ODR
; D 41FF 22 06          COPYXA R6 -> Acc
; D 4201 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4204 C9             SEROUT                             the digit
; D 4205 42 0A          INCX R10
; D 4207 86 0A 00 01    TESTXI R10 0001
; D 420B A1 02 16       IFFALSEI OD2
; D 420E 11 0E 05 2F    LOADXI R14 052F
; D 4212 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       3.
; D 4214 BE 00          RETURN
; OD2:
; D 4216 87 A9          TESTXY R10 = R9
; D 4218 A0 02 46       IFTRUEI ODR                        the last one: no gap after it
; D 421B 23 00 A6       COPYXY R10 -> R6
; D 421E 43 06          DECX R6
; D 4220 11 0E 00 32    LOADXI R14 0032
; D 4224 4D 6E          DIVXY R6 / R14
; D 4226 27             COPYREMA
; D 4227 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 422A A1 02 35       IFFALSEI OD3
; D 422D 11 0E 05 33    LOADXI R14 0533
; D 4231 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       fifty to a line
; D 4233 BE 00          RETURN
; OD3:
; D 4235 21 06          COPYAX Acc -> R6
; D 4237 4D 6F          DIVXY R6 / R15
; D 4239 27             COPYREMA
; D 423A 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 423D A1 02 46       IFFALSEI ODR
; D 4240 11 0E 05 31    LOADXI R14 0531
; D 4244 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       groups of ten
; ODR:
; D 4246 BE 00          RETURN
; NUM:
; D 4248 4D AF          DIVXY R10 / R15
; D 424A 27             COPYREMA
; D 424B 21 0C          COPYAX Acc -> R12
; D 424D 25             COPYMAA
; D 424E 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10                  RC = units, RA = n / 10
; D 4250 2E 0C 06 04    READIDX R12 0604
; D 4254 2F 0B 06 6B    WRITEIDX R11 066B
; D 4258 4D AF          DIVXY R10 / R15
; D 425A 27             COPYREMA
; D 425B 21 0C          COPYAX Acc -> R12
; D 425D 25             COPYMAA
; D 425E 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10                  RC = tens, RA = hundreds and up (< 100)
; D 4260 2E 0C 06 04    READIDX R12 0604
; D 4264 2F 0B 06 6A    WRITEIDX R11 066A
; D 4268 2E 0A 06 04    READIDX R10 0604
; D 426C 2F 0B 06 69    WRITEIDX R11 0669
; D 4270 2E 0A 05 A0    READIDX R10 05A0
; D 4274 2F 0B 06 68    WRITEIDX R11 0668
; D 4278 11 0C 00 00    LOADXI R12 0000
; NZ:
; D 427C 2E 0C 06 68    READIDX R12 0668
; D 4280 81 00 30       TESTAI 0030
; D 4283 A1 02 8F       IFFALSEI NP                        the first digit that is not 0
; D 4286 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4288 86 0C 00 03    TESTXI R12 0003
; D 428C A1 02 7C       IFFALSEI NZ                        (the last digit always prints)
; NP:
; D 428F 11 0E 06 68    LOADXI R14 0668
; D 4293 50 EC 0E       ADDXYZ R14 + R12 -> R14
; D 4296 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4298 BE 00          RETURN
; PARSE:
; D 429A 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000
; D 429E 11 0C 00 00    LOADXI R12 0000
; D 42A2 11 0D 00 00    LOADXI R13 0000
; PS:
; D 42A6 2E 0C 06 6E    READIDX R12 066E
; D 42AA 21 0E          COPYAX Acc -> R14
; D 42AC 8C 0E          TESTXZ R14
; D 42AE A0 02 FB       IFTRUEI PR                         end of the line
; D 42B1 86 0E 00 20    TESTXI R14 0020
; D 42B5 A1 02 C2       IFFALSEI PDG
; D 42B8 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 42BA 8C 0D          TESTXZ R13
; D 42BC A0 02 A6       IFTRUEI PS                         spaces before the number
; D 42BF B0 02 E0       GAL PT
; PDG:
; D 42C2 53 0E 00 30    SUBXI R14 0030
; D 42C6 89 EF          TESTLXY R14 < R15
; D 42C8 A1 02 F7       IFFALSEI PBAD                      not a digit
; D 42CB 42 0D          INCX R13
; D 42CD 86 0D 00 05    TESTXI R13 0005
; D 42D1 A0 02 F7       IFTRUEI PBAD                       five digits: too long
; D 42D4 4A AF          MULTXY R10 * R15
; D 42D6 21 1A          COPYAX MA -> R10
; D 42D8 50 AE 0A       ADDXYZ R10 + R14 -> R10            n = n x 10 + digit
; D 42DB 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 42DD B0 02 A6       GAL PS
; PT:
; D 42E0 2E 0C 06 6E    READIDX R12 066E
; D 42E4 21 0E          COPYAX Acc -> R14
; D 42E6 8C 0E          TESTXZ R14
; D 42E8 A0 02 FB       IFTRUEI PR
; D 42EB 86 0E 00 20    TESTXI R14 0020
; D 42EF A1 02 F7       IFFALSEI PBAD
; D 42F2 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 42F4 B0 02 E0       GAL PT
; PBAD:
; D 42F7 11 0D FF FE    LOADXI R13 FFFE
; PR:
; D 42FB BE 00          RETURN

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; NATIVE CODE  -  a18 listing of Firmware-Math/pi_native.asm (commented out)
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;                                CPU     1802
;                        ; ==========================================================================
;                        ;  PI BY THE SPIGOT - one pass of the spigot, in raw 1802, called by $F1 RUNMC
;                        ; ==========================================================================
;                        ;  The bytecode version spends ~4,350 1802 instructions on each array term
;                        ;  (16 STELLAR opcodes, mostly dispatch and SCRT). Here a term is ~170.
;                        ;
;                        ;  TWO ENTRIES (absolute addresses - RUNMC operands are not program-relative):
;                        ;    INIT  $4700   a[1..L] = 2              L = the word at LW
;                        ;    PASS  $4730   one pass from i = TOP down to 1:
;                        ;                      x = 10 a[i] + q i;  a[i] = x mod (2i-1);  q = x div (2i-1)
;                        ;                  then a[1] = q mod 10 and DIGIT = q div 10
;                        ;
;                        ;  THE ARRAY: a[i] is a big-endian word at ARR + 2i. ARR is even, so every
;                        ;  high byte is at an even address - and $5000 and $6000 (the first bytes of
;                        ;  the VM2 and VM3 blocks this program borrows with SETSIZE 3) only ever hold a
;                        ;  HIGH byte. a[i] < 2i - 1 < 10000, so that byte is never $CD (START): a cold
;                        ;  boot can never mistake stale array data for a VM2/VM3 program.
;                        ;
;                        ;  ARITHMETIC: x is 24 bits (RD.0 : RB) - past ~480 digits 10 a + q i passes
;                        ;  65535. q is always < 128 (measured: at most 103 for up to 1500 digits).
;                        ;  NO MULTIPLY: d = 2i - 1, so q i = (q div 2) d + (q div 2) + (i if q is odd),
;                        ;  and the division only has to count y = 10 a + (q div 2) [+ i] in d's - at
;                        ;  most about 11, on average about 5 - starting from q div 2.
;                        ;
;                        ;  CALLING CONVENTION (the RUNMC handler at $2600, see gol_native.asm):
;                        ;    P = R3; R6 is the way home; return with D5. R2, R7-R9, RB, RD-RF are
;                        ;    saved and restored by the handler; RA is avoided. X is not preserved:
;                        ;    SEX R2 before returning.
;                        ;
;                        ;  REGISTERS:  R7 -> a[i] (its high byte)   R8 i   R9 d = 2i - 1
;                        ;              RB x low 16                   RD.0 x high byte   RD.1 q
;                        ;              RE -> D0 (d in memory)        RF -> I0 (i in memory)
;                        ; ==========================================================================
;
;   4810                 ARR     EQU     SCR+16          ; a[i] at ARR + 2i (a[0] unused)
;
;                        ; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;                        ;  INIT: a[1..L] = 2.     RUNMC $4700
;                        ; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;   4700                         ORG     04700H
;   4700   f8 48         INIT:   LDI     HIGH LWH
;   4702   bf                    PHI     R15
;   4703   f8 06                 LDI     LOW LWH
;   4705   af                    PLO     R15
;   4706   4f                    LDA     R15
;   4707   b8                    PHI     R8
;   4708   0f                    LDN     R15
;   4709   a8                    PLO     R8                      ; R8 = L
;   470a   f8 48                 LDI     HIGH (ARR+2)
;   470c   b7                    PHI     R7
;   470d   f8 12                 LDI     LOW (ARR+2)
;   470f   a7                    PLO     R7                      ; R7 -> a[1]
;   4710   f8 00         FILL:   LDI     000H
;   4712   57                    STR     R7
;   4713   17                    INC     R7
;   4714   f8 02                 LDI     002H
;   4716   57                    STR     R7
;   4717   17                    INC     R7
;   4718   28                    DEC     R8
;   4719   88                    GLO     R8
;   471a   3a 10                 BNZ     FILL
;   471c   98                    GHI     R8
;   471d   3a 10                 BNZ     FILL
;   471f   e2                    SEX     R2
;   4720   d5                    DB      0D5H                    ; RETURN
;
;                        ; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;                        ;  PASS.     RUNMC $4730
;                        ; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;   4730                         ORG     04730H
;   4730   f8 48         PASS:   LDI     HIGH TOPH
;   4732   bf                    PHI     R15
;   4733   f8 04                 LDI     LOW TOPH
;   4735   af                    PLO     R15
;   4736   4f                    LDA     R15
;   4737   b8                    PHI     R8
;   4738   0f                    LDN     R15
;   4739   a8                    PLO     R8                      ; R8 = i = TOP
;   473a   88                    GLO     R8
;   473b   fe                    SHL
;   473c   a9                    PLO     R9
;   473d   98                    GHI     R8
;   473e   7e                    SHLC
;   473f   b9                    PHI     R9                      ; R9 = 2i
;   4740   89                    GLO     R9
;   4741   fc 10                 ADI     LOW ARR
;   4743   a7                    PLO     R7
;   4744   99                    GHI     R9
;   4745   7c 48                 ADCI    HIGH ARR
;   4747   b7                    PHI     R7                      ; R7 = ARR + 2i -> a[i]
;   4748   29                    DEC     R9                      ; R9 = d = 2i - 1
;   4749   f8 48                 LDI     HIGH I0
;   474b   bf                    PHI     R15
;   474c   be                    PHI     R14
;   474d   f8 01                 LDI     LOW I0
;   474f   af                    PLO     R15                     ; RF -> I0
;   4750   f8 03                 LDI     LOW D0
;   4752   ae                    PLO     R14                     ; RE -> D0
;   4753   f8 00                 LDI     000H
;   4755   bd                    PHI     R13                     ; q = 0
;
;   4756   47            TERM:   LDA     R7
;   4757   bb                    PHI     R11
;   4758   07                    LDN     R7
;   4759   ab                    PLO     R11                     ; x = a[i]   (R7 -> its low byte)
;   475a   f8 00                 LDI     000H
;   475c   ad                    PLO     R13
;   475d   8b                    GLO     R11                     ; x <<= 2: 4a
;   475e   fe                    SHL
;   475f   ab                    PLO     R11
;   4760   9b                    GHI     R11
;   4761   7e                    SHLC
;   4762   bb                    PHI     R11
;   4763   8d                    GLO     R13
;   4764   7e                    SHLC
;   4765   ad                    PLO     R13
;   4766   8b                    GLO     R11
;   4767   fe                    SHL
;   4768   ab                    PLO     R11
;   4769   9b                    GHI     R11
;   476a   7e                    SHLC
;   476b   bb                    PHI     R11
;   476c   8d                    GLO     R13
;   476d   7e                    SHLC
;   476e   ad                    PLO     R13
;   476f   e7                    SEX     R7                      ; x += a: 5a   (a is still at R7)
;   4770   8b                    GLO     R11
;   4771   f4                    ADD
;   4772   ab                    PLO     R11
;   4773   27                    DEC     R7                      ; R7 -> the high byte again
;   4774   9b                    GHI     R11
;   4775   74                    ADC
;   4776   bb                    PHI     R11
;   4777   8d                    GLO     R13
;   4778   7c 00                 ADCI    000H
;   477a   ad                    PLO     R13
;   477b   8b                    GLO     R11                     ; x <<= 1: 10a
;   477c   fe                    SHL
;   477d   ab                    PLO     R11
;   477e   9b                    GHI     R11
;   477f   7e                    SHLC
;   4780   bb                    PHI     R11
;   4781   8d                    GLO     R13
;   4782   7e                    SHLC
;   4783   ad                    PLO     R13
;                                ; ---- x += q i, with no multiply. d = 2i - 1, so with h = q div 2:
;                                ;   q i = h d + h + (i if q is odd)
;                                ; and x div d = h + y div d, x mod d = y mod d, where
;                                ;   y = 10 a + h + (i if q is odd)          (y < 12 d: a short count)
